<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Computes the exact homogeneous steady state (R*, G*) = (a + rho_G, rho_G/(a+rho_G)^2) and Schnakenberg Turing dispersion relation Re(lambda(k)) (L33-77), backed by 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_055_gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney.lean`. However, it does not numerically integrate the 2D coupled mesenchymal GDNF + epithelial RET + Wnt11 + Sprouty1 reaction-diffusion PDEs or grow a spatial ureteric tree, and omits the Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- renal agenesis negative control." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L80–L97: Uses ideal 2^g tip power law without coupled reaction-diffusion PDE or growing ureteric tree solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L80-L97>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

